const validationHTML=document(`<main class="container py-4"><h1>Practice registration validation</h1><form id="registrationForm" novalidate><label class="form-label" for="studentName">Student name</label><input id="studentName" class="form-control" required maxlength="100" aria-describedby="nameFeedback"><div class="invalid-feedback" id="nameFeedback">Enter a name of 1–100 characters.</div><label class="form-label mt-3" for="studentEmail">Practice email</label><input id="studentEmail" type="email" class="form-control" required aria-describedby="emailFeedback"><div class="invalid-feedback" id="emailFeedback">Enter a valid fictional email format.</div><button class="btn btn-primary mt-3" type="submit">Validate practice form</button></form><button id="helpTip" class="btn btn-outline-secondary mt-3" data-bs-toggle="tooltip" title="No backend or email delivery is connected">Form help</button><button id="helpPopover" class="btn btn-outline-secondary mt-3" data-bs-toggle="popover" title="Practice" data-bs-content="Use fictional data only.">More information</button><p id="formStatus" role="status"></p><div class="progress mt-3" role="progressbar" aria-label="Practice setup" aria-valuenow="50" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100"><div class="progress-bar" style="width:50%">50%</div></div>${toast}</main>`);
const validationJS=`document.getElementById('registrationForm').addEventListener('submit',event=>{
 event.preventDefault();const name=document.getElementById('studentName'),email=document.getElementById('studentEmail');
 const nameValid=name.value.trim().length>0&&name.value.trim().length<=100;const emailValid=/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/.test(email.value.trim());
 for(const [field,valid] of [[name,nameValid],[email,emailValid]]){field.classList.toggle('is-invalid',!valid);field.classList.toggle('is-valid',valid);field.setAttribute('aria-invalid',String(!valid));}
 document.getElementById('formStatus').textContent=nameValid&&emailValid?'Client checks passed; no server record was created.':'Review the named fields.';
 if(nameValid&&emailValid)bootstrap.Toast.getOrCreateInstance(document.getElementById('statusToast'),{autohide:false}).show();
});`;
add('Form Validation and Interactive Components','is-valid/invalid; feedback; was-validated; HTML5/novalidate; client+server; tooltip/popover/toast/spinner/progress',
 'Bootstrap styles do not validate or secure data. Native HTML constraints provide browser checks; novalidate disables automatic submission-time constraint UI so custom code must validate and report errors accessibly. .was-validated styles native :valid/:invalid states; explicit .is-invalid/.is-valid reflect supplied validation state. Connect feedback to fields and provide text/status rather than color alone. Bootstrap documents accessibility limits in custom validation styles; test with assistive technology and prefer native validation where practical. Tooltips/popovers require initialization; the trusted preview initializes configured ones. Toasts should use appropriate live regions and not hide important information. Spinners need loading text and progress bars need values/labels.',validationHTML,
 'Create a labeled student-registration form with clear validation feedback. After successful client checks show a toast or alert, explicitly stating no backend is connected. Compare native constraints and novalidate, add spinner/loading text and explain real server-side validation requirements.',
 [['Does Bootstrap styling replace server validation?','No','Always','Only with is-valid','Only with cards'],['What does novalidate disable?','Automatic native submission constraint UI','All possible JS checks','Every form label','Server authorization'],['What marks a supplied invalid state?','is-invalid','Only fw-bold','A private credential','navbar-expand-md'],['What do tooltips generally require?','Initialization and suitable triggers','A production database','A plaintext password','jQuery in Bootstrap 5'],['What should a spinner include?','Accessible loading text','Only movement','Only color','A hidden token']],{js:validationJS});
const uiHTML=(login=false)=>document(`${nav}<main id="home" class="container-fluid py-4"><h1>Student Information UI</h1><div class="alert alert-warning" role="status">Front-end practice only: no secure authentication, backend or persistent records. Changes reset on Run.</div>${login?'<section class="card mb-4" aria-labelledby="loginTitle"><div class="card-body"><h2 id="loginTitle" class="h5">Login view · mockup only</h2><form id="demoLogin"><label for="demoUser" class="form-label">Username</label><input id="demoUser" class="form-control" placeholder="Fictional username"><label for="demoPassword" class="form-label mt-2">Password field demonstration</label><input id="demoPassword" class="form-control" type="password" placeholder="Do not enter a real password"><button class="btn btn-outline-primary mt-3" type="submit">Preview login feedback</button><p id="loginFeedback" role="status"></p></form></div></section>':''}<div class="row g-3"><aside class="col-lg-3">${offcanvas}<nav class="list-group mt-3" aria-label="Dashboard sections"><a href="#students" class="list-group-item list-group-item-action">Students</a><a href="#reports" class="list-group-item list-group-item-action">Reports</a></nav></aside><div class="col-lg-9"><section id="reports" class="row g-3" aria-label="Statistics"><div class="col-12 col-md-4">${card('Total students','<span id="studentCount">0</span>')}</div><div class="col-12 col-md-4">${card('Passing','<span id="passingCount">0</span>')}</div><div class="col-12 col-md-4">${card('Practice courses','IT · CS')}</div></section><section id="students" class="mt-4"><h2>Student management</h2><div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-end gap-2"><div><label for="studentSearch" class="form-label">Search by name</label><input id="studentSearch" class="form-control" type="search"></div><div><label for="courseFilter" class="form-label">Course</label><select id="courseFilter" class="form-select"><option value="">All</option><option>IT</option><option>CS</option></select></div><div><label for="sortOrder" class="form-label">Sort</label><select id="sortOrder" class="form-select"><option value="name">Name</option><option value="grade">Grade descending</option></select></div><button id="addStudentButton" class="btn btn-primary">Add Student</button></div><p id="listStatus" role="status" class="mt-3"></p><div class="table-responsive" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Student list"><table class="table table-striped"><caption>Fictional in-memory students</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">ID</th><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Course</th><th scope="col">Grade</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Actions</th></tr></thead><tbody id="studentRows"></tbody></table></div><nav aria-label="Student list pages"><div class="d-flex gap-2"><button id="previousPage" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Previous</button><span id="pageLabel" class="align-self-center"></span><button id="nextPage" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next</button></div></nav></section><section class="mt-4"><h2>Student cards</h2><div id="studentCards" class="row g-3"></div></section></div></div>${modal('studentModal','Add / Edit Student','<form id="studentForm" novalidate><label for="recordName" class="form-label">Name</label><input id="recordName" class="form-control" maxlength="100" required><label for="recordCourse" class="form-label mt-2">Course</label><select id="recordCourse" class="form-select"><option>IT</option><option>CS</option></select><label for="recordGrade" class="form-label mt-2">Grade</label><input id="recordGrade" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="0.1" class="form-control" required><p id="recordError" role="alert"></p><button class="btn btn-primary mt-3" type="submit">Save in-memory record</button></form>')}${modal('deleteModal','Confirm practice deletion','<p id="deleteText"></p><button id="confirmDelete" class="btn btn-danger">Confirm delete</button>')}${modal('detailModal','Student details','<div id="detailContent"></div>')}${toast}</main>`);
const uiJS=`let students=[{id:1,name:'Maria Santos',course:'IT',grade:91},{id:2,name:'Joel Cruz',course:'CS',grade:72},{id:3,name:'Ana Reyes',course:'IT',grade:85}];
let editing=null,deleting=null,page=1;const pageSize=2;
const byId=id=>document.getElementById(id);
const notify=text=>{byId('toastMessage').textContent=text;bootstrap.Toast.getOrCreateInstance(byId('statusToast'),{autohide:false}).show();};
const open=(type,id)=>bootstrap[type].getOrCreateInstance(byId(id),{toggle:false});
function render(){
 const search=byId('studentSearch').value.trim().toLowerCase(),course=byId('courseFilter').value;
 const result=students.filter(s=>s.name.toLowerCase().includes(search)&&(!course||s.course===course)).sort((a,b)=>byId('sortOrder').value==='grade'?b.grade-a.grade:a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
 const pages=Math.max(1,Math.ceil(result.length/pageSize));page=Math.min(Math.max(page,1),pages);const visible=result.slice((page-1)*pageSize,page*pageSize);
 byId('studentRows').replaceChildren();byId('studentCards').replaceChildren();
 byId('studentCount').textContent=String(students.length);byId('passingCount').textContent=String(students.filter(s=>s.grade>=75).length);
 byId('listStatus').textContent=result.length?result.length+' matching fictional records':'No students match. Try another search/filter.';
 byId('pageLabel').textContent='Page '+page+' of '+pages;byId('previousPage').disabled=page<=1;byId('nextPage').disabled=page>=pages;
 for(const s of visible){
  const row=document.createElement('tr');for(const value of [s.id,s.name,s.course,s.grade,s.grade>=75?'Passed':'Needs support']){const cell=document.createElement('td');cell.textContent=String(value);row.append(cell);}
  const actions=document.createElement('td');for(const [label,handler] of [['Details',()=>{byId('detailContent').textContent=s.name+' · '+s.course+' · grade '+s.grade;open('Modal','detailModal').show();}],['Edit',()=>{editing=s.id;byId('recordName').value=s.name;byId('recordCourse').value=s.course;byId('recordGrade').value=String(s.grade);byId('recordError').textContent='';open('Modal','studentModal').show();}],['Delete',()=>{deleting=s.id;byId('deleteText').textContent='Delete fictional record '+s.name+'?';open('Modal','deleteModal').show();}]]){const button=document.createElement('button');button.type='button';button.className='btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary me-1';button.textContent=label;button.addEventListener('click',handler);actions.append(button);}row.append(actions);byId('studentRows').append(row);
  const column=document.createElement('div');column.className='col-12 col-md-6';const card=document.createElement('article');card.className='card card-body h-100';const heading=document.createElement('h3');heading.className='h5';heading.textContent=s.name;const text=document.createElement('p');text.textContent=s.course+' · '+s.grade;card.append(heading,text);column.append(card);byId('studentCards').append(column);
 }
}
byId('studentSearch').addEventListener('input',()=>{page=1;render();});for(const id of ['courseFilter','sortOrder'])byId(id).addEventListener('change',()=>{page=1;render();});
byId('previousPage').addEventListener('click',()=>{page--;render();});byId('nextPage').addEventListener('click',()=>{page++;render();});
byId('addStudentButton').addEventListener('click',()=>{editing=null;byId('recordName').value='';byId('recordCourse').value='IT';byId('recordGrade').value='';byId('recordError').textContent='';open('Modal','studentModal').show();});
byId('studentForm').addEventListener('submit',event=>{event.preventDefault();const name=byId('recordName').value.trim(),course=byId('recordCourse').value,raw=byId('recordGrade').value.trim(),grade=Number(raw);if(!name||name.length>100||!['IT','CS'].includes(course)||!raw||!Number.isFinite(grade)||grade<0||grade>100){byId('recordError').textContent='Enter a name, IT/CS course and grade from 0 to 100.';return;}if(editing!==null)students=students.map(s=>s.id===editing?{...s,name,course,grade}:s);else{if(students.length>=100){byId('recordError').textContent='Practice limit: 100 records.';return;}students.push({id:Math.max(0,...students.map(s=>s.id))+1,name,course,grade});}open('Modal','studentModal').hide();render();notify('Practice record updated in memory only.');});
byId('confirmDelete').addEventListener('click',()=>{students=students.filter(s=>s.id!==deleting);deleting=null;open('Modal','deleteModal').hide();render();notify('Practice record deleted from memory only.');});
byId('demoLogin')?.addEventListener('submit',event=>{event.preventDefault();byId('demoPassword').value='';byId('loginFeedback').textContent='Login UI preview only. No user is authenticated.';});
render();console.log('Fictional UI ready. All changes reset on Run.');`;
add('Intermediate Project — Student Registration Dashboard','navbar/sidebar/offcanvas; statistics; registration/table; add/edit modal; alerts/validation/badges/pagination; responsive UI',
 'Build an original front-end dashboard using in-memory fictional records. The reference supports add/edit/delete confirmation, search/filter/sort, page controls and statistics through a limited Bootstrap component bridge. No database, secure login or durable persistence is connected. Extend the layout with status badges, registration feedback and an accessible loading/empty/error experience. Pagination controls manipulate the sample list rather than pretending to fetch a server page.',uiHTML(),
 'Milestones: responsive shell → cards/sidebar → form/table → Add/Edit modal → input validation → in-memory rendering/search → pagination → alerts/toast → delete confirmation → keyboard/responsive tests. Test valid/invalid names/grades, canceled deletion, search with no matches, page bounds, long text, mobile offcanvas and focus return. Submit original files and actual test evidence; label all changes as UI-only.',
 [['Where are practice records stored?','In memory for this Run','CodeLab production DB','A secure backend automatically','A permanent cloud store'],['What must precede deletion?','Confirmation','Any search','Only a hover','A password in HTML'],['What should pagination demonstrate?','Real sample-list page behavior or clearly labeled UI','Fake server persistence','A secret token','No current-page information'],['What validates real application records?','Server checks plus appropriate client checks','Only Bootstrap colors','Only a button label','Only CSS'],['What should no matches show?','A useful empty state','A broken table only','A fabricated student','A credential']],{project:true,js:uiJS});
add('Bootstrap Customization','CSS variables/custom properties; themes/overrides/utilities; Sass/source/variables/Utility API; separate custom CSS',
 'Level 1 uses separate custom CSS loaded after Bootstrap: override appropriate component variables and selectors while retaining readable focus/contrast. Changing --bs-primary alone does not recolor every precompiled .btn-primary rule, so set component variables intentionally. Level 2 uses Bootstrap Sass sources and a separate Sass build to change variables/maps and generate utilities; the browser preview does not compile Sass. Do not edit distributed bootstrap.min.css. Keep a documented palette and reuse focused classes rather than many unrelated !important overrides.',
 document(`<main class="container py-4 school-theme"><h1>Practice school theme</h1><nav class="school-nav rounded p-3 mb-3" aria-label="Theme navigation"><a class="text-white" href="#themeCard">Profile</a></nav><article id="themeCard" class="card"><div class="card-body"><h2 class="h5">Consistent palette</h2><button class="btn btn-primary">Primary action</button><button class="btn btn-outline-secondary ms-2">Secondary action</button><label for="themeName" class="form-label d-block mt-3">Student name</label><input id="themeName" class="form-control"></div></article></main>`),
 'Create primary/secondary colors, buttons, navbar, cards and visible form focus styles in custom CSS. Document a Sass variable/Utility API build plan separately; explain which styles can be changed at runtime and which need compilation.',
 [['Where should overrides go?','Separate custom CSS or a build process','Edited distributed CSS','Laravel .env','A plaintext password'],['Does changing --bs-primary recolor every compiled component automatically?','No','Always','Only when logged in','Only with jQuery'],['What builds Sass sources?','A separate Sass compiler/build','The CSS editor automatically','A SQL engine','A password hasher'],['What must a new palette retain?','Readable contrast and focus','Only decoration','Only one color','Invisible labels'],['What creates custom Bootstrap utilities in a build?','The Utility API','A database login','A modal ID','The grid caption']],{css:'.school-theme{--school-primary:#16324f;--school-secondary:#526579}.school-nav{background:var(--school-primary)}.school-theme .btn-primary{--bs-btn-bg:#16324f;--bs-btn-border-color:#16324f;--bs-btn-hover-bg:#244969;--bs-btn-hover-border-color:#244969}.school-theme .form-control:focus{border-color:#16324f;box-shadow:0 0 0 .25rem rgba(22,50,79,.25)}'});
add('Advanced Responsive Design','mobile-first; adaptive spacing/typography/navigation/tables/forms; reading order/show-hide/touch; multi-viewport tests',
 'Responsive design is more than adding a breakpoint class. Test content at 375, 768, 1280 and larger widths, keyboard zoom and long/localized text. Keep touch targets comfortably spaced, tables scrollable and labels readable. Visual reordering must not create a confusing keyboard/reading order. Bootstrap has responsive spacing/display/grid utilities; custom fluid typography such as clamp can complement them. Avoid hiding important information simply to make a mobile screenshot fit.',profile,
 'Redesign a desktop-only portal for phone, tablet, laptop and large desktop. Document layout changes, responsive navigation/table/form behavior, touch targets, reading order, visible focus and zoom/reflow checks.',
 [['What should responsive testing include?','Actual content and interactions at multiple widths','Only a class list','Only one desktop image','Disabling zoom'],['What should visual order respect?','Meaningful DOM and keyboard order','Random placement','Only color','A password'],['How can a wide data table remain usable?','A labeled keyboard-scrollable responsive wrapper','Tiny unreadable text','Deleting all headers','Hiding all values'],['What should remain visible on phones?','Essential information/actions','Only decoration','Only the footer','No error messages'],['What is clamp useful for?','Bounded fluid CSS values','Authentication','Database writes','Sass compilation in a browser']]);
add('Bootstrap with JavaScript','component APIs/instances; programmatic modal/toast/collapse/dropdown/tooltip/popover; events/shown/hidden',
 'Bootstrap exposes component constructors and static getOrCreateInstance/getInstance methods. show/hide are asynchronous transitions, so lifecycle events are the right place for post-transition actions. In CodeLab supported component methods become commands to the trusted preview; they do not give student code a native parent window. Use a unique ID on each programmatically controlled component. Test shown.bs.modal and hidden.bs.modal as well as close controls; do not assume show returns after a transition finishes. Arbitrary plugin internals/native measurements are outside this bridge.',
 document(`<main class="container py-4"><h1>Programmatic student details</h1><button id="openDetails" type="button" class="btn btn-primary">View Maria’s details</button><p id="modalStatus" role="status"></p>${modal('detailModal','Student details','<p id="studentDescription"></p>')}</main>`),
 'Select fictional student data, safely populate the modal description, open it through bootstrap.Modal and update a status message on shown/hidden lifecycle events. Add a programmatic toast and explain transition timing.',
 [['Which reuses or creates an instance?','getOrCreateInstance','alwaysNewOnly','queryPassword','jQueryRequired'],['When is the modal transition finished?','At shown.bs.modal','Immediately on every show return','Before the element exists','Only after SQL'],['What should identify a bridge-controlled component?','A unique element ID','Only a color','A private token','The same duplicate ID everywhere'],['How should plain untrusted text be assigned?','textContent','Unfiltered innerHTML','A script tag','A query string token'],['What does the bridge provide?','Limited trusted component commands in the isolated preview','Full parent DOM access','Application cookies','Native arbitrary JS execution']],{js:`const element=document.getElementById('detailModal');const details=bootstrap.Modal.getOrCreateInstance(element);document.getElementById('openDetails').addEventListener('click',()=>{document.getElementById('studentDescription').textContent='Maria Santos · IT · Grade 91';details.show();});element.addEventListener('shown.bs.modal',()=>{document.getElementById('modalStatus').textContent='Student details opened.';});element.addEventListener('hidden.bs.modal',()=>{document.getElementById('modalStatus').textContent='Student details closed.';});`});
